        "original_id": "fe56e424-8564-50e5-874b-b99e21a79eea",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Nicholas Ray, Elia Kazan, Jerry Wald, Norman Krasna, David Dortort, Horace McCoy, Alfred Hayes, Andrew Solt, Claude Stanush\n- Works: Rebel Without a Cause, The Lusty Men\n- Roles: film director, director, producer, writer, actor, screenwriter, novelist\n- Organizations: The New York Times\n\nFacts:\n- Elia Kazan was born as Elias Kazantzoglou on September 7, 1909.\n- Nicholas Ray was born as Raymond Nicholas Kienzle Jr. on August 7, 1911.\n- The Lusty Men was directed by Nicholas Ray.\n- The Lusty Men was produced by Jerry Wald and Norman Krasna.\n- The Lusty Men had a screenplay by David Dortort, Horace McCoy, Alfred Hayes, Andrew Solt, and Jerry Wald.\n- The Lusty Men was based on a novel by Claude Stanush.\n- Nicholas Ray was an American film director best known for the movie Rebel Without a Cause.\n- Nicholas Ray died on June 16, 1979.\n- Elia Kazan was a Greek-American director, producer, writer, and actor.\n- The New York Times described Elia Kazan as one of the most honored and influential directors in Broadway and Hollywood history.\n- Elia Kazan died on September 28, 2003.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
